1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,505
The air can't keep
up with the ground.

2
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:04,865
But the air has a problem.

3
00:00:05,048 --> 00:00:07,453
The ground speeds
up at once;

4
00:00:07,453 --> 00:00:11,273
the atmosphere is pulled
along only by friction,

5
00:00:11,298 --> 00:00:12,933
and that takes time.

6
00:00:13,187 --> 00:00:16,257
For the first hours,
the air is left behind.

7
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:19,670
At a 12 hour day,
the ground is moving

8
00:00:19,670 --> 00:00:23,645
through the air
at about 460 meters

9
00:00:23,645 --> 00:00:27,035
a second, faster
than the speed of sound.

10
00:00:27,415 --> 00:00:32,285
That is about
1,670 kilometers an hour.

11
00:00:32,515 --> 00:00:36,055
The strongest gust ever
measured by a weather

12
00:00:36,055 --> 00:00:40,785
station was about
408 kilometers an hour.

13
00:00:41,053 --> 00:00:44,388
So this wind would be
about four times stronger.

14
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:47,540
And it would blow
from the east, because

15
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:50,345
the ground is running
ahead of the air.

16
00:00:50,585 --> 00:00:51,840
Hang on.

17
00:00:51,945 --> 00:00:54,765
If you're enjoying this,
tap like and follow.

18
00:00:54,975 --> 00:00:56,700
Okay, back to the math.

19
00:00:57,248 --> 00:01:00,043
Winds like that would
strip the surface,

20
00:01:00,128 --> 00:01:02,298
and they would only
be the beginning.

21
00:01:02,613 --> 00:01:04,913
And then the oceans
start to move.

22
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:06,730
Part three of eight.
